crc32: slicing-by-8 for short inputs and for the tails of Chorba

Short inputs previously used braid or the small Chorba variant with a braid tail, depending on length and
alignment. The byte-wise part of braid waits for each table load on the in-order C906. Slicing-by-8
(crc32_slice8_tbl.h, eight 1 KiB tables) takes eight bytes per step from one unaligned 64-bit load. Chorba's
small variants finish with the same code. Chorba stays from 176 bytes on, where it is faster. The CRC is
unchanged.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/crc32_slice8_tbl.h
@@ -0,0 +1,370 @@
